  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PROTECTION RESTORATION &amp; MANAGEMENT OF C</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will support objectives identified by the North American Waterfowl Management Plan for Northern Pintail, Lesser Scaup, Blue-winged Teal, Green-winged Teal, Northern Shoveler, Brant, Snowy Plover, Red Knot, and Marbled Godwit, through a variety of activities in three priority wetlands in northwest Mexico: Baha Santa Mara, Ensenada de Pabellones, and Marismas Nacionales Biosphere Reserve. It will improve the protection of 5,224.7 acres through the establishment of Private Natural Protected Areas and the creation of conservation management units. It will restore 91 acres, dredge 2.25 miles of a river; restore 6.5 miles of channels; and manage habitat on 1.8 miles and 747 acres. It will also conduct bird monitoring and environmental education in the communities.</narrative>
  </description>
